IN ORDER TO LOOK IN THAT CAMERA
AND MAKE PEOPLE WANT YOU

223
00:08:36,816 --> 00:08:38,684
TO SELL THEIR PRODUCT.

224
00:08:38,684 --> 00:08:40,820
Tyra: I'VE DONE EXERCISES
WITH TASHA WHERE I'M CRYIN'

225
00:08:40,820 --> 00:08:44,024
AND SCREAMIN' AND DON'T KNOW
HOW SHE GOT THAT OUT OF ME.

226
00:08:44,024 --> 00:08:45,792
THAT ONLY MAKES ME
A BETTER MODEL, AND IT MAKES ME

227
00:08:45,792 --> 00:08:47,594
A BETTER ACTRESS.

228
00:08:47,594 --> 00:08:49,896
Tasha: SO, TYRA?
Tyra: BYE, Y'ALL!

229
00:08:49,896 --> 00:08:50,964
BYE, MISS TASHA.

230
00:08:50,964 --> 00:08:52,565
Tasha: THANK YOU, SISTA!
MWAH!

231
00:08:52,565 --> 00:08:54,768
BYE, YOU GUYS.

232
00:08:54,768 --> 00:08:57,137
Tasha: AND NOW YOU'RE ALL
IN MY HANDS.

233
00:08:57,137 --> 00:08:59,105
Sara: WHEN TYRA LEAVES,
IT'S A WHOLE OTHER BALL GAME.

234
00:08:59,105 --> 00:09:02,675
SHE'S LIKE,
"OKAY, WE'RE GONNA GET DIRTY."

235
00:09:02,675 --> 00:09:04,044
Tasha: WHAT MAKES US
REALLY GOOD ACTORS

236
00:09:04,044 --> 00:09:08,982
IS THAT WE'RE ABLE TO LOCATE
EACH INDIVIDUAL EMOTIONAL THING

237
00:09:08,982 --> 00:09:11,551
AND UTILIZE IT AS A TOOL.

238
00:09:11,551 --> 00:09:16,189
SO TODAY WHAT I WANNA REALLY
TRY TO WORK ON IS BEING OPEN

239
00:09:16,189 --> 00:09:18,058
AND BEING HONEST.

240
00:09:18,058 --> 00:09:20,660
I'M JUST GONNA GIVE YOU GUYS
THIS PIECE OF PAPER, OKAY?

241
00:09:22,562 --> 00:09:24,164
AND LET'S JUST TALK ABOUT
REJECTION, BECAUSE THAT'S WHAT

242
00:09:24,164 --> 00:09:26,199
SOME OF YOU ARE GONNA HAVE
TO DEAL WITH--REJECTION.

243
00:09:26,199 --> 00:09:27,967
YOU KNOW HOW IT FEELS?

244
00:09:27,967 --> 00:09:29,102
HOW MANY OF YOU HAVE EVER HAD
A BOYFRIEND THAT BROKE UP

245
00:09:29,102 --> 00:09:32,138
WITH YOU?

246
00:09:32,138 --> 00:09:34,140
A DADDY THAT LEFT YOU?

247
00:09:34,140 --> 00:09:38,111
IMAGINE THAT IS
A "DEAR JOHN" LETTER

248
00:09:38,111 --> 00:09:43,083
FROM WHOEVER THAT PERSON IS
THAT YOU FELT REJECTED YOU

249
00:09:43,083 --> 00:09:44,484
AND LEFT YOU.

250
00:09:44,484 --> 00:09:46,886
LOOK AT IT.

251
00:09:46,886 --> 00:09:48,888
YOU SEE THE EMOTIONS
THAT'S COMING UP?

252
00:09:48,888 --> 00:09:50,557
Sara: IT'S, LIKE, WEIRD
BECAUSE YOU'RE LOOKIN' AT

253
00:09:50,557 --> 00:09:53,526
A BLANK PIECE OF PAPER,
BUT IT HAS SO MUCH ON IT.

254
00:09:53,526 --> 00:09:54,861
♪♪♪

255
00:09:56,996 --> 00:09:59,866
April: EMOTIONS, TO ME,
ARE UNCONTROLLABLE.

256
00:09:59,866 --> 00:10:03,002
WHEN I OPEN MYSELF UP TO THEM,
THERE ARE TEARS IMMEDIATELY,

257
00:10:03,002 --> 00:10:05,772
AND IT'S, LIKE... (sighs)

258
00:10:05,772 --> 00:10:08,875
Tasha: LOOK AT IT.

259
00:10:08,875 --> 00:10:11,211
NOW I WANT YOU TO RIP
THAT PIECE OF PAPER UP

260
00:10:11,211 --> 00:10:12,779
IN LITTLE TEENY PIECES.

261
00:10:12,779 --> 00:10:15,715
RIP IT UP! RIP IT UP! RIP IT UP!

262
00:10:15,715 --> 00:10:17,016
STOP!

263
00:10:17,016 --> 00:10:19,552
NOW ALL OF YOU RIGHT NOW
ARE HURTING.

264
00:10:19,552 --> 00:10:22,222
ALL OF YOU RIGHT NOW
MAY BE FEELING ANGER,

265
00:10:22,222 --> 00:10:24,724
HURT, PAIN.

266
00:10:24,724 --> 00:10:27,760
DON'T FORGET WHAT YOU'RE FEELING
RIGHT NOW, BECAUSE YOU'RE GONNA

267
00:10:27,760 --> 00:10:30,864
HAVE OPPORTUNITIES TO USE THIS.

268
00:10:30,864 --> 00:10:33,266
IF YOU'RE WORKING TO TRY
TO ACCOMPLISH A CAREER

269
00:10:33,266 --> 00:10:34,901
AS AN ACTOR-- HELLO.

270
00:10:34,901 --> 00:10:36,136
Camille: HI. HOW ARE YOU?
Tasha: SO WE HAVE

271
00:10:36,136 --> 00:10:37,570
A NEW PERSON COMING IN.

272
00:10:37,570 --> 00:10:38,872
WHAT'S YOUR NAME?

273
00:10:38,872 --> 00:10:40,173
Camille: CAMILLE.
Tasha: HI, CAMILLE.

274
00:10:40,173 --> 00:10:42,242
Camille: I'M SLOWLY LOOKING
AT EVERYONE'S FACES,

275
00:10:42,242 --> 00:10:46,679
REALIZING THAT PEOPLE ARE KIND
OF SAD AND CRYING AND QUIET.

276
00:10:46,679 --> 00:10:50,083
SO I'M JUST LIKE,
OH... MY... GOD.

277
00:10:52,051 --> 00:10:53,486
Tasha: WHAT IS IT
THAT YOU'RE FEELING RIGHT NOW?

278
00:10:53,486 --> 00:10:55,855
LIKE, WHAT'S THE THING THAT
MADE YOU BREAK DOWN AND CRY?

279
00:10:55,855 --> 00:10:57,257
Sara: MY DAD.

280
00:10:57,257 --> 00:11:01,828
MY FATHER JUST HAS THIS MINDSET
THAT MODELING IS NOT THE JOB

281
00:11:01,828 --> 00:11:02,996
FOR A DAUGHTER.

282
00:11:02,996 --> 00:11:04,797
Tasha: I NEED YOU
TO LOOK AT HER

283
00:11:04,797 --> 00:11:07,267
AND SAY TO YOUR FATHER
EVERYTHING THAT YOU'VE WANTED

284
00:11:07,267 --> 00:11:09,802
TO SAY ABOUT HOW HE'S HURT YOU.

285
00:11:09,802 --> 00:11:14,040
I WANT YOU TO REPEAT EVERYTHING
THAT SHE SAYS QUIETLY, OKAY?

286
00:11:14,040 --> 00:11:16,009
BEGIN TO TALK.

287
00:11:16,009 --> 00:11:18,077
Sara: I'M DOING THIS,
BUT IF YOU DISOWN ME--

288
00:11:18,077 --> 00:11:19,212
I'M GONNA BE A MODEL.

289
00:11:19,212 --> 00:11:20,213
Mercedes: I'M GONNA BE
A MODEL.

290
00:11:20,213 --> 00:11:21,548
Sara: YOU CAN HATE ME.

291
00:11:21,548 --> 00:11:23,583
Mercedes: YOU CAN DO
WHATEVER YOU WANNA DO...

292
00:11:23,583 --> 00:11:25,151
Sara: IT'S KIND OF LIKE
AN OUT-OF-BODY EXPERIENCE,

293
00:11:25,151 --> 00:11:28,555
AND I'M FEELING JUST THIS ENERGY
AROUND US.

294
00:11:28,555 --> 00:11:30,857
Shandi: I DON'T KNOW ANYONE
IN MY FAMILY BECAUSE OF YOU.

295
00:11:30,857 --> 00:11:32,559
I HATE YOU.

296
00:11:32,559 --> 00:11:34,160
Catie: AND THERE WERE TIMES
I DID NOT WANNA LIVE BECAUSE

297
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:35,828
OF YOUR (bleep) FACE.

298
00:11:35,828 --> 00:11:37,897
April: YOUR (bleep) FACE.

299
00:11:37,897 --> 00:11:39,732
Mercedes: I DIDN'T THINK
WE WERE GONNA GET THIS HEAVY

300
00:11:39,732 --> 00:11:41,901
THE FIRST DAY,
BUT THIS WHOLE LESSON

301
00:11:41,901 --> 00:11:44,804
WAS TO TEACH YOU
TO BE HONEST AND VULNERABLE.

302
00:11:44,804 --> 00:11:47,874
April: I'M SO TIRED...
Catie: I'M SO TIRED.

303
00:11:47,874 --> 00:11:50,009
April: OF BEING BRAVE...
Catie: OF BEING BRAVE...

304
00:11:50,009 --> 00:11:53,646
April: OR FOR...
Women: (crying)

305
00:11:57,584 --> 00:11:58,885
Sara: WE'RE LETTING
JUST ALL OF THESE, YOU KNOW,

306
00:11:58,885 --> 00:12:01,754
EMOTIONS IN OUR PERSONAL LIVES
OUT.

307
00:12:01,754 --> 00:12:05,858
Mercedes: (sobbing)
Sara: (sobbing)

308
00:12:05,858 --> 00:12:07,193
AND CAMILLE'S THE ONLY ONE
THAT'S NOT AFFECTED

309
00:12:07,193 --> 00:12:08,861
BY ANY OF THIS.

310
00:12:08,861 --> 00:12:10,129
Camille: MOM,
YOU'RE MY STRENGTH.

311
00:12:10,129 --> 00:12:11,497
Yoanna: MOM,
YOU'RE MY STRENGTH.

312
00:12:11,497 --> 00:12:12,131
Camille: I LOVE YOU.
Yoanna: I LOVE YOU.

313
00:12:12,131 --> 00:12:13,833
Tasha: STOP.

314
00:12:13,833 --> 00:12:15,735
I WANT YOU TO DEAL WITH
THE THINGS THAT ARE NOT SO EASY.

315
00:12:15,735 --> 00:12:17,103
LET'S CHANGE IT.

316
00:12:17,103 --> 00:12:19,072
ARE YOU ANGRY AT ANYBODY?

317
00:12:19,072 --> 00:12:20,773
Camille: I'M NOT ANGRY
AT ANYONE.

318
00:12:20,773 --> 00:12:23,109
Tasha: NO?
Camille: I THINK...

319
00:12:23,109 --> 00:12:25,778
Yoanna: (scoffs)
Tasha: YOU?

320
00:12:25,778 --> 00:12:26,980
THAT'S INTERESTING.

321
00:12:26,980 --> 00:12:28,181
LOOK IN HER EYES.

322
00:12:28,181 --> 00:12:30,883
AND OBVIOUSLY,
YOU DID SOMETHING TO HER, TOO.

323
00:12:30,883 --> 00:12:33,119
SO WE MAY AS WELL GET IT ALL OUT
RIGHT NOW.

324
00:12:33,119 --> 00:12:34,520
Yoanna: OKAY, LET'S GO.

325
00:12:34,520 --> 00:12:35,822
Tasha: OKAY,
SO YOU HAVE TO REPEAT HER.

326
00:12:35,822 --> 00:12:36,889
Camille: IN THE HOUSE,
I FELT LIKE YOU WERE

327
00:12:36,889 --> 00:12:38,691
TARNISHING MY CHARACTER.

328
00:12:38,691 --> 00:12:40,526
IT HURT BECAUSE...
Yoanna: IT HURT BECAUSE...

329
00:12:40,526 --> 00:12:41,894
Tasha: BE HONEST, CAMILLE.

330
00:12:41,894 --> 00:12:44,063
THIS IS YOUR OPPORTUNITY
TO JUST BE HONEST.

331
00:12:44,063 --> 00:12:45,765
Camille: IT HURT BECAUSE
Yoanna: BECAUSE...

332
00:12:45,765 --> 00:12:46,633
Camille: I'M IN
A NEW ENVIRONMENT

333
00:12:46,633 --> 00:12:48,067
