442
00:16:32,057 --> 00:16:34,059
Catie: WHOSE HUSBAND
WAS IN THE MILITARY.

443
00:16:34,059 --> 00:16:35,494
April: SHE THINKS HE'S DEAD.

444
00:16:35,494 --> 00:16:36,928
Shandi: SO SHE MOVES ON.
Catie: AND HE COMES BACK.

445
00:16:36,928 --> 00:16:38,864
Tasha: ACTION.

446
00:16:38,864 --> 00:16:41,900
April: I DIDN'T BELIEVE IT
WHEN THEY TOLD ME,

447
00:16:41,900 --> 00:16:43,802
BUT IT'S TRUE.

448
00:16:43,802 --> 00:16:44,970
Sara: I DIDN'T BELIEVE IT
WHEN THEY TOLD ME,

449
00:16:44,970 --> 00:16:46,038
BUT IT'S TRUE.

450
00:16:46,038 --> 00:16:47,706
Catie: IT'S TRUE.
YOU'RE ALIVE.

451
00:16:47,706 --> 00:16:48,874
Yoanna: YOU KNOW,
WHEN THEY TOLD ME THAT

452
00:16:48,874 --> 00:16:50,442
YOUR PLANE WENT DOWN
IN THE JUNGLE AND THAT

453
00:16:50,442 --> 00:16:51,910
THERE WERE NO SURVIVORS...

454
00:16:51,910 --> 00:16:53,011
Sara: WHEN THEY GAVE ME
THAT FLAG THEY DRAPED

455
00:16:53,011 --> 00:16:55,680
OVER YOUR COFFIN...

456
00:16:55,680 --> 00:16:57,783
Mercedes: I PUT IT
UNDER MY PILLOW...

457
00:16:57,783 --> 00:17:00,952
April: AND I CRIED MYSELF
TO SLEEP EVERY NIGHT

458
00:17:00,952 --> 00:17:03,722
FOR SIX MONTHS.

459
00:17:03,722 --> 00:17:05,390
Mark: APRIL'S DOING
A GREAT JOB.

460
00:17:05,390 --> 00:17:06,758
I BELIEVED IN HER EYES.

461
00:17:06,758 --> 00:17:09,795
SHE WAS BEING TRUTHFUL
TO THE SITUATION.

462
00:17:09,795 --> 00:17:12,830
Shandi: AND I CRIED MYSELF
TO SLEEP EVERY NIGHT

463
00:17:12,830 --> 00:17:14,566
FOR SIX MONTHS.

464
00:17:14,566 --> 00:17:17,102
Mark: SHANDI IS SHOWING
AN OPENNESS.

465
00:17:17,102 --> 00:17:19,003
I SAW IT IN HER EYES.

466
00:17:19,003 --> 00:17:21,039
THERE WAS THIS CONNECTION
THAT SHE HAD THAT A LOT OF

467
00:17:21,039 --> 00:17:22,674
OTHER PEOPLE DIDN'T HAVE.

468
00:17:22,674 --> 00:17:23,742
Catie: WHEN THEY TOLD ME
YOUR PLANE WENT DOWN

469
00:17:23,742 --> 00:17:26,611
IN THE JUNGLE...

470
00:17:26,611 --> 00:17:28,947
AND THERE WERE NO SURVIVORS,
I DIDN'T SHED A TEAR.

471
00:17:28,947 --> 00:17:31,716
Mark: CATIE--
SHE'S SHOWING YOU EVERYTHING

472
00:17:31,716 --> 00:17:34,086
BUT NOT FEELING ANYTHING,
WHICH MAKES IT

473
00:17:34,086 --> 00:17:35,153
NOT VERY BELIEVABLE.

474
00:17:35,153 --> 00:17:36,555
Mark: (suppresses chuckle)

475
00:17:36,555 --> 00:17:38,723
Catie: AND THEN I--
AND THEN I MET A MAN.

476
00:17:38,723 --> 00:17:40,158
I'M HALF-ASSING IT.

477
00:17:40,158 --> 00:17:42,127
HOW THE CRAP
CAN I TAKE THIS SERIOUSLY?

478
00:17:42,127 --> 00:17:43,895
I'M NOT FEELING THIS GUY.

479
00:17:43,895 --> 00:17:46,164
AND HE MADE ME REALIZE
I COULD LIVE AGAIN.

480
00:17:46,164 --> 00:17:49,568
Sara: AND I CRIED MYSELF
TO SLEEP FOR SIX MONTHS.

481
00:17:49,568 --> 00:17:51,703
Mercedes: CRIED MYSELF
TO SLEEP FOR SIX MONTHS.

482
00:17:51,703 --> 00:17:56,041
Camille: I CRIED, COLIN,
NOT FOR ONE, NOT FOR TWO,

483
00:17:56,041 --> 00:17:59,044
BUT I CRIED FOR SIX MONTHS.

484
00:17:59,044 --> 00:18:01,980
Mark: CAMILLE HAS TAKEN IT
UPON HERSELF TO CHANGE

485
00:18:01,980 --> 00:18:04,382
A LOT OF THE LINES,
WHICH JUST REALLY

486
00:18:04,382 --> 00:18:05,784
SHOULDN'T HAPPEN.

487
00:18:05,784 --> 00:18:10,055
Camille: YOU KNOW ME--
LAURA, STRONG AND PROUD,

488
00:18:10,055 --> 00:18:12,023
THE ONE THAT YOU LOVED
AND RESPECTED.

489
00:18:12,023 --> 00:18:15,494
I'M APPROACHING THE SCENE
WITH THE FACT THAT I'M

490
00:18:15,494 --> 00:18:17,796
GONNA BE ME, WHICH IS UNIQUE.

491
00:18:17,796 --> 00:18:19,531
(stilted voice) I DIDN'T
BELIEVE IT.

492
00:18:19,531 --> 00:18:21,700
IT'S TRUE. YOU ARE ALIVE.

493
00:18:21,700 --> 00:18:24,703
I FOCUSED MY ENERGY
INTO SCULPTING.

494
00:18:24,703 --> 00:18:26,004
I EVEN GAVE SOME AWAY
TO CHARITY.

495
00:18:28,573 --> 00:18:29,574
Yoanna: AT THE END,
THERE'S SUPPOSED TO BE

496
00:18:29,574 --> 00:18:30,642
A PASSIONATE KISS.

497
00:18:30,642 --> 00:18:32,611
April: I LOVE YOU.

498
00:18:32,611 --> 00:18:35,413
I ALWAYS HAVE,
AND I ALWAYS WILL.

499
00:18:35,413 --> 00:18:36,681
♪♪♪

500
00:18:43,121 --> 00:18:44,422
Shandi: THIS IS
THE END OF THE SCENE--

501
00:18:44,422 --> 00:18:45,757
PASSIONATELY KISS.

502
00:18:45,757 --> 00:18:48,026
TO ME, PASSIONATE IS TONGUE,
SO THERE YOU GO.

503
00:18:49,961 --> 00:18:50,962
Yoanna: WHAT DO YOU EXPECT?

504
00:18:50,962 --> 00:18:52,531
WE'VE BEEN STUCK
WITH 12 GIRLS.

505
00:18:52,531 --> 00:18:54,733
IT WAS TIME
FOR SOME TESTOSTERONE.

506
00:18:54,733 --> 00:18:57,135
Catie: WE HAVE TO KISS
THIS PERSON.

507
00:18:59,971 --> 00:19:01,873
ECCH!

508
00:19:01,873 --> 00:19:03,375
UGH!

509
00:19:05,677 --> 00:19:06,912
Tasha: YOU COULD'VE
KISSED HIM BETTER THAN THAT.

510
00:19:06,912 --> 00:19:08,413
Catie: I CAN'T,
I HAVE A BOYFRIEND.

511
00:19:08,413 --> 00:19:09,614
SORRY.
Tasha: SO WHAT?

512
00:19:09,614 --> 00:19:10,782
THIS IS ABOUT WINNING.

513
00:19:10,782 --> 00:19:12,584
YOU HAVE TO STAY COMMITTED
IN THE SCENE.

514
00:19:12,584 --> 00:19:13,919
IF YOU'RE THINKING ABOUT
YOUR BOYFRIEND,

515
00:19:13,919 --> 00:19:16,621
ONLY HALF OF YOUR HEART'S
GONNA BE IN THIS SCENE.

516
00:19:16,621 --> 00:19:18,123
Catie: MM, OKAY.

517
00:19:18,123 --> 00:19:20,025
Camille: I LOVE YOU SO MUCH.

518
00:19:20,025 --> 00:19:23,562
WHY DID YOU HAVE TO
LEAVE ME?

519
00:19:23,562 --> 00:19:26,531
WHY DID YOU HAVE TO LEAVE ME,
BABY?

520
00:19:26,531 --> 00:19:28,466
(sniffling)

521
00:19:35,140 --> 00:19:39,010
Tasha: BEFORE I SAY ANYTHING,
MARK, I'LL GIVE YOU THE HONORS

522
00:19:39,010 --> 00:19:41,646
TO SAY SOMETHING FIRST.

523
00:19:41,646 --> 00:19:42,881
Mark: YOU DO SOMETHING
FOR DAVID MAMET

524
00:19:42,881 --> 00:19:45,850
OR SOMEBODY LIKE THAT,
YOU CHANGE THEIR WORDS,

525
00:19:45,850 --> 00:19:48,587
YOU WON'T HAVE THAT JOB ANYMORE,
I PROMISE YOU THAT.

526
00:19:48,587 --> 00:19:50,622
Tasha: I DON'T KNOW
IF YOU FEEL LIKE YOU'VE LEARNED

527
00:19:50,622 --> 00:19:53,825
SOMETHING BETWEEN TODAY
AND YESTERDAY.

528
00:19:53,825 --> 00:19:55,827
I DIDN'T BELIEVE ANYTHING
YOU DID UP THERE.

529
00:19:55,827 --> 00:19:57,028
NOTHING.

530
00:19:57,028 --> 00:19:58,430
I THOUGHT IT WAS HORRIBLE.

531
00:19:58,430 --> 00:19:59,798
Camille: I THOUGHT
I DID WELL.

532
00:19:59,798 --> 00:20:02,934
I RESPECT HER,
BUT SHE HAS TO UNDERSTAND THAT

533
00:20:02,934 --> 00:20:04,369
DIFFERENT PEOPLE ARE DIFFERENT.

534
00:20:04,369 --> 00:20:06,805
Tasha: (sighs)
POOR CAMILLE.

535
00:20:06,805 --> 00:20:07,772
SHE'S CLUELESS.

536
00:20:14,675 --> 00:20:15,676
(horn honks)

537
00:20:17,144 --> 00:20:19,313
Tasha: CAN WE HAVE
ALL OF OUR LADIES COME OUT

538
00:20:19,313 --> 00:20:21,648
ONTO THE STAGE, PLEASE?

539
00:20:21,648 --> 00:20:24,084
DID YOU SEE HOW IMPORTANT
YESTERDAY WAS

540
00:20:24,084 --> 00:20:27,321
TO REALLY ACCOMPLISH THE GOAL
OF TODAY?

541
00:20:27,321 --> 00:20:28,755
IT WAS REALLY INTERESTING.

542
00:20:28,755 --> 00:20:30,724
DID YOU LEARN SOMETHING?

543
00:20:30,724 --> 00:20:35,095
CAMILLE, YOU WERE NOT AFFECTED,
AND YOU REFUSED TO BE AFFECTED.

544
00:20:35,095 --> 00:20:36,797
I SAY GET AFFECTED.

545
00:20:36,797 --> 00:20:37,898
GET AFFECTED.

546
00:20:37,898 --> 00:20:40,133
CATIE, YOU KNOW HOW HARD
YOU WORKED

547
00:20:40,133 --> 00:20:41,702
AND HOW HARD YOU DIDN'T.

548
00:20:41,702 --> 00:20:45,239
SOMETIMES YOU MAY GIVE UP
BEFORE IT'S OVER,

549
00:20:45,239 --> 00:20:48,342
AND IF YOU DO THAT,
YOU AUTOMATICALLY LOSE.

550
00:20:48,342 --> 00:20:50,310
Catie: MM-HMM.
Mark: APRIL AND SHANDI,

551
00:20:50,310 --> 00:20:51,945
TO ME, WERE THE BEST.

552
00:20:51,945 --> 00:20:55,015
Tasha: YOU GUYS WERE
THE BEST, THE TOP OF THE LINE,

553
00:20:55,015 --> 00:20:58,852
BUT UNFORTUNATELY,
THERE CAN ONLY BE ONE WINNER,

554
00:20:58,852 --> 00:21:01,388
AND THE WINNER IS...

555
00:21:01,388 --> 00:21:03,156
Mark: APRIL.

556
00:21:03,156 --> 00:21:05,025
Tasha: YOU ALLOWED
ALL YOUR INNER EMOTIONS

557
00:21:05,025 --> 00:21:06,159
TO COME OUT.

558
00:21:06,159 --> 00:21:07,828
YOU DIDN'T TRY TO HOLD BACK.

559
00:21:07,828 --> 00:21:10,097
April: THE POSITIVE FEEDBACK
FELT REALLY GOOD TO ME

560
00:21:10,097 --> 00:21:12,633
BECAUSE ONE OF THE PROBLEMS
I THINK I'VE BEEN HAVING

561
00:21:12,633 --> 00:21:14,268
IS LETTING THE REAL ME
COME THROUGH.

562
00:21:14,268 --> 00:21:19,873
Tasha: THE PRIZE...
IS A FABULOUS SHOPPING SPREE

563
00:21:19,873 --> 00:21:24,111
AT ONE OF THE TOP JEWELRY STORES
IN NEW YORK CITY.

564
00:21:24,111 --> 00:21:26,146
YOU GET TO PICK SOMEBODY
TO GO WITH.

565
00:21:26,146 --> 00:21:27,981
April: CATIE.

566
00:21:27,981 --> 00:21:30,284
CATIE IS 18 YEARS OLD.

567
00:21:30,284 --> 00:21:34,855
SHE'S--SHE'S STILL A TEENAGER,
AND HONESTLY, WHEN I'M WITH HER,

568
00:21:34,855 --> 00:21:36,657
I FEEL LIKE I'M 18, TOO,

569
00:21:36,657 --> 00:21:38,625
SO I WANTED TO BRING HER
WITH ME.

570
00:21:38,625 --> 00:21:39,960
Catie: I'M SO EXCITED.

571
00:21:39,960 --> 00:21:41,762
WE'RE GONNA GET HER
SOME GOOD JEWELRY,

572
00:21:41,762 --> 00:21:43,163
GET HER SOME BLING.

573
00:21:43,163 --> 00:21:44,164
♪♪♪

574
00:21:47,167 --> 00:21:49,536
Camille: TODAY WAS, UM,
A BAD DAY ACCORDING TO,

575
00:21:49,536 --> 00:21:53,173
YOU KNOW, THE PEOPLE
I'M GETTING CRITIQUED BY

576
00:21:53,173 --> 00:21:56,209
BECAUSE THEY SAY THAT
I'M KIND OF, LIKE, UNATTACHED,

577
00:21:56,209 --> 00:21:59,246
LIKE, I'M NOT, LIKE, EMOTIONAL.

578
00:21:59,246 --> 00:22:00,547
Catie: SHOULD I SAY HI
TO HIM?

579
00:22:00,547 --> 00:22:02,182
HOW COME YOU'VE NEVER CRIED
IN FRONT OF CAMILLE?

580
00:22:02,182 --> 00:22:03,884
SHE'S VERY EMOTIONALLY DETACHED.

581
00:22:03,884 --> 00:22:05,419
Camille's dad: (chuckles)

582
00:22:05,419 --> 00:22:07,054
Catie: I JUST WANNA SEE
THAT THIS GIRL'S HUMAN.

583
00:22:07,054 --> 00:22:08,355
Camille's dad: Okay, then.

584
00:22:08,355 --> 00:22:09,756
Catie: BECAUSE US GIRLS ARE

585
00:22:09,756 --> 00:22:11,658
♪ EMOTIONAL ♪♪

586
00:22:11,658 --> 00:22:14,428
SHOW ME SOME EMOTION!

587
00:22:16,363 --> 00:22:18,031
Mercedes: WHEN YOU GET
ALL THIS CRITICISM

588
00:22:18,031 --> 00:22:20,701
FROM THE JUDGES AND STUFF,
HOW DO YOU HANDLE THAT?

589
00:22:20,701 --> 00:22:22,369
Camille: I THINK OF IT

590
00:22:22,369 --> 00:22:23,670
AS BEING POSITIVE.

591
00:22:23,670 --> 00:22:25,172
LIKE, I DON'T THINK OF IT--

592
00:22:25,172 --> 00:22:26,607
Mercedes: IT'S NOT REALLY
POSITIVE INFORMATION.

593
00:22:26,607 --> 00:22:28,775
THE ONLY WAY FOR HER
TO HANDLE CRITICISM

594
00:22:28,775 --> 00:22:31,778
IS TO BE HARD, TOUGH
AND DOMINATE THE SITUATION.

595
00:22:31,778 --> 00:22:32,679
Camille: SUPPOSEDLY,
I'M THE WORST OUT OF, LIKE,

596
00:22:32,679 --> 00:22:34,481
EVERYONE ELSE.

597
00:22:34,481 --> 00:22:36,249
IT'S OKAY, 'CAUSE IF I WANT
TO DO THE ACTING THING,

598
00:22:36,249 --> 00:22:37,417
I WILL DO THE ACTING THING.

599
00:22:37,417 --> 00:22:38,652
Mercedes: SO PLEASE VOTE
FOR CAMILLE.

600
00:22:38,652 --> 00:22:39,686
Camille: THAT'S IT.

601
00:22:39,686 --> 00:22:41,154
Mercedes: SHE'S RUNNING
FOR OFFICE.

602
00:22:41,154 --> 00:22:43,624
SHE WANTS THAT CONTROL 24/7,
AND SHE JUST FEELS LIKE

603
00:22:43,624 --> 00:22:46,660
IF SHE LOSES THAT CONTROL,
SHE WON'T BE ABLE TO WIN.

604
00:22:46,660 --> 00:22:48,161
Camille: (scoffs)
I'M GOOD, SO...

605
00:22:51,131 --> 00:22:53,400
April: COME ON, DARLIN'!

606
00:22:53,400 --> 00:22:55,636
Catie: GOD, THEY PICKED
THE PERFECT PRIZE FOR THIS DAY.

607
00:22:55,636 --> 00:22:56,570
April: I'M SO EXCITED.

608
00:23:00,607 --> 00:23:01,575
H. STERN.

609
00:23:01,575 --> 00:23:03,443
Catie: AAH!

610
00:23:03,443 --> 00:23:04,745
April: HI!

611
00:23:04,745 --> 00:23:07,547
I FEEL LIKE A LITTLE GIRL
IN A CANDY STORE

612
00:23:07,547 --> 00:23:09,783
WHO JUST GETS TO PICK
WHAT SHE WANTS.

613
00:23:09,783 --> 00:23:12,052
I LIKE THOSE EARRINGS,
THAT NECKLACE.

614
00:23:12,052 --> 00:23:13,720
WHAT A FABULOUS NIGHT
FROM START TO FINISH

615
00:23:13,720 --> 00:23:16,189
TO BE ABLE TO PERFORM ONSTAGE
FOR THE FIRST TIME,

616
00:23:16,189 --> 00:23:17,791
AND THEN TO HAVE IT TOPPED OFF
WITH THIS.

617
00:23:17,791 --> 00:23:19,226
PINCH ME, PINCH ME.

618
00:23:19,226 --> 00:23:20,293
IT'S INCREDIBLE.

619
00:23:20,293 --> 00:23:22,162
THESE ARE PERFECT FOR ME. YEAH.

620
00:23:22,162 --> 00:23:24,531
Catie: YEAH, OKAY. YAY!
April: THANK YOU SO MUCH.

621
00:23:24,531 --> 00:23:26,366
TAKE CARE.
Woman: BYE.

622
00:23:26,366 --> 00:23:27,601
HAVE A GOOD NIGHT. TAKE CARE.

623
00:23:30,404 --> 00:23:32,039
Yoanna: TYRA MAIL!

624
00:23:32,039 --> 00:23:33,573
"TOMORROW WE'LL SEE WHO
WILL FIGHT THE BEST FIGHT

625
00:23:33,573 --> 00:23:35,275
TO BE AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

626
00:23:35,275 --> 00:23:37,411
BE READY TO LEAVE
AT 6 IN THE MORNING."

627
00:23:37,411 --> 00:23:38,512
Camille: WHAT?
Catie: SHE'S GONNA FIGHT US.

628
00:23:38,512 --> 00:23:40,781
Yoanna: ARE WE GONNA BOX?
Mercedes: I DON'T WANNA

629
00:23:40,781 --> 00:23:42,516
KICK TYRA'S BUTT.

630
00:23:42,516 --> 00:23:43,550
Catie: WE'LL SEE TOMORROW.

631
00:23:43,550 --> 00:23:44,418
WE'LL FIND OUT.

632
00:23:45,686 --> 00:23:46,787
(alarm clock beeping)

633
00:23:57,197 --> 00:23:58,699
Catie: YUCK.

634
00:23:58,699 --> 00:24:00,100
THIS IS HEALTHY OATMEAL.

635
00:24:02,803 --> 00:24:04,504
Sara: IS IT THAT BAD?
Catie: DISGUSTING.

636
00:24:06,306 --> 00:24:09,242
Sara: MMM, IT'S GOOD.
Catie: ECCH.

637
00:24:09,242 --> 00:24:10,510
♪♪♪

638
00:24:11,912 --> 00:24:13,046
April: THE TYRA MAIL
WAS PRETTY VAGUE,

639
00:24:13,046 --> 00:24:15,916
SO WE JUST ARE READY
FOR ANYTHING.

640
00:24:15,916 --> 00:24:18,985
♪♪♪

641
00:24:18,985 --> 00:24:20,954
Jay: GOOD MORNING.

642
00:24:20,954 --> 00:24:23,023
TODAY YOU'RE DOING
A TELEVISION COMMERCIAL

643
00:24:23,023 --> 00:24:25,292
FOR ROLLITOS CHIPS.

644
00:24:25,292 --> 00:24:27,327
Sara: OH, MY GOD.

645
00:24:27,327 --> 00:24:29,129
Jay: YOU GIRLS HAVE
THE PRIVILEGE TO WORK WITH

646
00:24:29,129 --> 00:24:31,732
A TALENTED DIRECTOR AND OWNER
OF MOST REMARKABLE FILMS,

647
00:24:31,732 --> 00:24:32,699
JAMES GAY.

648
00:24:32,699 --> 00:24:34,067
JAMES, COME OUT AND SAY HEY.

649
00:24:34,067 --> 00:24:35,936
James: WE HAVE A SCRIPT
TO GET THROUGH, WHICH IS

650
00:24:35,936 --> 00:24:37,137
A LITTLE DIFFERENT FOR YOU GUYS.

651
00:24:37,137 --> 00:24:38,271
WE HAVE A LOT TO DO,
SO THERE'S NO TIME

652
00:24:38,271 --> 00:24:40,073
TO BE NERVOUS.

653
00:24:40,073 --> 00:24:42,008
Jay: ACTUALLY, TODAY WE'RE
AT THE DARYL ROTH THEATRE,

654
00:24:42,008 --> 00:24:43,944
HOME OF THE SHOW "DE LA GUARDA."

655
00:24:43,944 --> 00:24:45,345
SO WE'RE GONNA DO SOMETHING
A LITTLE DIFFERENT.

656
00:24:50,150 --> 00:24:52,219
Yoanna: OH, MY GOD! AAH!

657
00:24:52,219 --> 00:24:53,787
♪♪♪

658
00:24:56,123 --> 00:24:57,824
Catie: WE'RE DOING THAT?

659
00:24:57,824 --> 00:24:59,926
Jay: ESSENTIALLY,
THE IDEA IS YOU GIRLS

660
00:24:59,926 --> 00:25:02,229
ARE IN A ROUGH AND TUMBLE
AERIAL CATFIGHT

661
00:25:02,229 --> 00:25:05,265
FIGHTING TO BECOME
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL,

662
00:25:05,265 --> 00:25:07,868
BUT YOU'RE FIGHTING LIKE
THERE'S ONLY ONE BAG

663
00:25:07,868 --> 00:25:08,869
OF CHIPS LEFT.

664
00:25:08,869 --> 00:25:10,170
(laughter)

665
00:25:10,170 --> 00:25:13,173
Catie: I'M REALLY JUST
FOCUSING ON HOW ANGRY I AM

666
00:25:13,173 --> 00:25:15,175
THAT I'M PUT
IN THIS SITUATION AGAIN.

667
00:25:15,175 --> 00:25:17,144
BEFORE WE DID
THE SUSPENDING SHOOT,

668
00:25:17,144 --> 00:25:18,478
I HAD A NERVOUS BREAKDOWN.

669
00:25:18,478 --> 00:25:20,447
MY ULTIMATE FEAR IN LIFE
IS FALLING TO MY DEATH.

